WEBVTT

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.794
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:22.829 --> 00:00:23.837
Sammy.

00:00:24.296 --> 00:00:26.173
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can.

00:00:26.208 --> 00:00:27.055
Go!

00:00:29.885 --> 00:00:32.095
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.406
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:37.476 --> 00:00:38.650
This is dad's book.

00:00:38.685 --> 00:00:40.771
I think dad wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:00:40.806 --> 00:00:42.814
You know, saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:42.849 --> 00:00:44.399
The family business.

00:00:44.566 --> 00:00:45.866
I got to find dad.

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:48.153
That's the only thing I can think about.

00:02:16.341 --> 00:02:17.724
I know you're just doing your job

00:02:17.759 --> 00:02:20.073
But the police have
been here a week already.

00:02:20.108 --> 00:02:22.353
I don't see why we have
to go through this again.

00:02:22.388 --> 00:02:25.350
The more he tells the story
the more he believes it's true.

00:02:25.385 --> 00:02:26.809
Mrs. McKay.

00:02:28.597 --> 00:02:30.403
We know you spoke with
the local authorities.

00:02:30.538 --> 00:02:34.337
But this seems like a matter
for the State Police. So...

00:02:34.372 --> 00:02:37.003
Don't worry about how
crazy it sounds Evan.

00:02:37.038 --> 00:02:39.130
You just tell us what you saw.

00:02:39.165 --> 00:02:41.295
I was up late...

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:43.391
Watching TV.

00:02:43.426 --> 00:02:45.178
When I heard this...

00:02:45.213 --> 00:02:46.978
Weird noise.

00:02:47.013 --> 00:02:50.078
What did it sound like?

00:02:50.113 --> 00:02:53.144
It sounded like a monster.

00:02:54.604 --> 00:02:57.815
Tell the officers what
you were watching on TV.

00:02:57.850 --> 00:02:59.525
Um...

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:03.035
Godzilla versus Mothra.

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:05.093
That's my favorite Godzilla movie.

00:03:05.128 --> 00:03:07.081
So much better than the original?

00:03:07.116 --> 00:03:07.900
Totally.

00:03:07.935 --> 00:03:10.298
Yeah, he likes the remake.

00:03:10.488 --> 00:03:11.794
Yuck.

00:03:11.829 --> 00:03:13.513
That's what I mean.

00:03:15.917 --> 00:03:17.133
Evan?

00:03:17.559 --> 00:03:19.879
Did you see what this thing was?

00:03:19.914 --> 00:03:22.253
No, but I saw it grab Mr. Jenkins.

00:03:22.288 --> 00:03:24.592
It pulled him underneath the car.

00:03:24.993 --> 00:03:26.204
Then what?

00:03:28.131 --> 00:03:30.354
It took him away.

00:03:30.389 --> 00:03:33.621
I heard the monster leaving.

00:03:33.656 --> 00:03:36.527
It made this really scary sound.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:39.398
What did it sound like, Evan?

00:03:39.956 --> 00:03:44.111
Like this whining growl.

00:03:47.016 --> 00:03:48.449
Thanks for your time.

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:55.331
So the local police
have novel out foul play.

00:03:55.966 --> 00:03:57.798
Apparently there were signs of struggle.

00:03:58.572 --> 00:04:00.461
You know, they could be right.
Could just be a kidnapping.

00:04:01.196 --> 00:04:03.246
Maybe this isn't our kind of gig.

00:04:03.281 --> 00:04:04.765
Yeah, maybe not.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.214
Except for this.

00:04:06.249 --> 00:04:08.425
Dad marked the area, Dean.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:11.129
Possible hunting grounds
of a phantom attacker.

00:04:11.164 --> 00:04:12.971
Why would he even do that?

00:04:13.006 --> 00:04:17.260
Well, he found a lot of local folk law
about a dog figure that comes out at night,

00:04:17.295 --> 00:04:19.888
Grabs people then vanishes.

00:04:19.923 --> 00:04:21.521
He found this too.

00:04:21.556 --> 00:04:26.687
This county has more missing persons per
capital than anywhere else in the state.

00:04:27.104 --> 00:04:28.078
It is weird.

00:04:28.563 --> 00:04:29.450
Yeah.

00:04:29.523 --> 00:04:32.491
Don't phantom attackers usually
snatch people from their beds?

00:04:32.526 --> 00:04:34.044
Jenkins was taken from a parking lot.

00:04:34.079 --> 00:04:35.563
Well, there are all kinds, you know.

00:04:35.564 --> 00:04:39.908
Spring Hill Jack, Spanworm Gases,
they take people anywhere, anytime.

00:04:39.943 --> 00:04:42.077
Look, Dean. I don't know if
this is our kind of gig either...

00:04:42.112 --> 00:04:45.163
Yeah, you're right. We should
ask around more tomorrow.

00:04:45.198 --> 00:04:46.623
Right.

00:04:47.666 --> 00:04:50.043
I saw a motel about five miles back.

00:04:50.078 --> 00:04:51.593
Whoa, whoa, easy.

00:04:51.628 --> 00:04:53.547
Let's have another round?

00:04:53.713 --> 00:04:55.138
We should get an early start.

00:04:55.173 --> 00:04:58.343
Now, you really know how to
have fun, don't you Grandma?

00:05:00.261 --> 00:05:01.375
You're right.

00:05:02.463 --> 00:05:04.444
I'll meet you outside.
I'm gonna take a leak.

00:06:52.222 --> 00:06:53.605
Hey, hey.

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:56.519
Have you guys been outside? Around
here like the last hour or so?

00:06:57.936 --> 00:06:59.104
Sam?

00:07:01.815 --> 00:07:03.176
Sammy!

00:07:22.503 --> 00:07:24.088
Sam...

00:07:35.766 --> 00:07:38.811
So, what can we do for
you Officer Washington?

00:07:38.846 --> 00:07:40.736
I'm working a missing persons.

00:07:40.771 --> 00:07:43.899
I didn't know the Jenkins case was
being covered by the State Police?

00:07:43.934 --> 00:07:46.318
Uh, no, no. It's someone else.

00:07:46.353 --> 00:07:48.035
Actually it's my cousin.

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:51.198
We were having a few laughs at
this bar down by the highway.

00:07:51.233 --> 00:07:53.081
And I haven't seen him since.

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:56.060
Did your cousin have a drinking problem?

00:07:56.095 --> 00:07:58.661
Sam? Two beers and he's doing Karaoke.

00:07:58.903 --> 00:08:01.833
No, he wasn't drunk. He was taken.

00:08:03.794 --> 00:08:05.712
All right. What's his name?

00:08:05.747 --> 00:08:07.214
Winchester.

00:08:08.465 --> 00:08:09.966
Sam Winchester.

00:08:10.508 --> 00:08:11.694
Like the riffle?

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:13.387
Like the riffle.

00:08:13.512 --> 00:08:15.103
Winchester, Sam

00:08:20.018 --> 00:08:21.985
Samuel Winchester.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:27.651
So you know that his brother
Dean Winchester died in St. Louis.

00:08:27.818 --> 00:08:30.654
And it was excepted a murder.

00:08:31.251 --> 00:08:32.906
Yeah, Dean.

00:08:33.508 --> 00:08:35.701
Kind of the black sheep of the family.

00:08:35.736 --> 00:08:37.232
Handsome though.

00:08:42.259 --> 00:08:44.042
Well, he's not showing up
at any current field reports.

00:08:44.077 --> 00:08:46.155
I already have a lead.

00:08:46.816 --> 00:08:49.047
I saw surveillance
camera above the highway.

00:08:49.082 --> 00:08:50.582
County traffic cam.

00:08:50.617 --> 00:08:51.774
Right, yeah.

00:08:51.809 --> 00:08:53.427
I'm thinking the camera
picked up whatever took him.

00:08:53.462 --> 00:08:55.470
Oh, whoever.

00:08:57.230 --> 00:08:58.890
Well, I have access to
the traffic cam footage

00:08:58.925 --> 00:09:01.723
Down at the county
works department, but...

00:09:01.758 --> 00:09:04.521
Well... Let me tell
you this the right way.

00:09:04.556 --> 00:09:08.442
Won't you fill out...

00:09:09.178 --> 00:09:10.993
A missing persons report.

00:09:14.102 --> 00:09:15.949
And sit tight over here.

00:09:16.805 --> 00:09:18.243
Officer, look uh...

00:09:19.432 --> 00:09:20.516
He's family.

00:09:21.156 --> 00:09:22.170
And I kind of...

00:09:23.134 --> 00:09:24.131
Look out for the kid.

00:09:25.074 --> 00:09:26.439
You got to let me go with you.

00:09:26.944 --> 00:09:28.411
I'm sorry, I can't do that.

00:09:30.221 --> 00:09:31.729
Well, tell me something.

00:09:31.764 --> 00:09:34.642
Your county has a fair
share of missing persons.

00:09:34.677 --> 00:09:37.478
Any of them come back?

00:09:38.187 --> 00:09:41.816
Sam's my responsibility.
And he's coming back.

00:09:41.851 --> 00:09:44.151
I'm bringing him back.

00:10:30.556 --> 00:10:31.689
Greg.

00:10:31.724 --> 00:10:33.559
I think we've got something.

00:10:34.768 --> 00:10:36.979
These traffic cam take an
image every three seconds.

00:10:37.014 --> 00:10:39.279
It's part of the amber alert program.

00:10:39.314 --> 00:10:43.902
These images were all taken around
the time your cousin Sam disappeared.

00:10:44.653 --> 00:10:46.084
This really isn't what I'm looking for.

00:10:46.119 --> 00:10:46.812
Just wait, wait.

00:10:46.857 --> 00:10:48.038
Next one.

00:10:48.073 --> 00:10:51.201
This one was taken right
after Sam left the bar.

00:10:51.236 --> 00:10:53.996
Look at the back in at that thing.

00:10:54.663 --> 00:10:57.207
Now, look at the plates.

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:01.427
The plates look new. Probably stolen.

00:11:01.462 --> 00:11:05.716
So, whoever's driving that
rust bucket must be involved.

00:11:12.473 --> 00:11:13.673
Do you hear that engine?

00:11:13.708 --> 00:11:14.939
Yeah.

00:11:15.893 --> 00:11:18.812
Kind of a whining growl, isn't it?

00:11:19.229 --> 00:11:21.148
Sure.

00:11:23.525 --> 00:11:25.486
I'll be damned.

00:11:40.417 --> 00:11:42.294
You're alive?

00:11:43.128 --> 00:11:44.428
Hey, you okay?

00:11:44.463 --> 00:11:47.424
Does it look like I'm doing okay?

00:11:48.552 --> 00:11:49.655
Where are we?

00:11:49.690 --> 00:11:51.220
I don't know.

00:11:51.903 --> 00:11:53.103
Country, I think.

00:11:53.757 --> 00:11:55.328
Smells like the country.

00:11:56.002 --> 00:11:57.518
You're Jenkins, aren't you?

00:11:58.054 --> 00:11:58.977
Yeah.

00:12:00.835 --> 00:12:02.272
Wow, I was looking for you.

00:12:02.603 --> 00:12:03.400
Oh, yeah?

00:12:03.435 --> 00:12:04.197
Yeah.

00:12:04.232 --> 00:12:07.826
Well, no offense. But
this is a piss poor rescue.

00:12:07.861 --> 00:12:11.406
Well, my brother's out there right
now too. He's looking for us. So...

00:12:11.441 --> 00:12:13.551
So, he's not gonna find us.

00:12:13.586 --> 00:12:15.626
We're in the middle of nowhere.

00:12:15.661 --> 00:12:18.580
Waiting for them to come back
and do God knows what to us.

00:12:18.615 --> 00:12:20.339
What are they?

00:12:21.061 --> 00:12:21.775
Have you seen them?

00:12:22.476 --> 00:12:22.702
What are you talking about?

00:12:22.703 --> 00:12:24.586
Whatever grabbed us,
what did they look like?

00:12:24.621 --> 00:12:26.338
See for yourself.

00:12:45.482 --> 00:12:46.615
Leave me alone.

00:12:47.384 --> 00:12:49.278
Don't touch me. Leave me alone!

00:13:06.619 --> 00:13:08.788
I'll be damned.

00:13:11.624 --> 00:13:13.216
They're just people.

00:13:13.251 --> 00:13:16.504
Yeah, what did you expect?

00:13:16.921 --> 00:13:18.568
How often do they feed you?

00:13:18.603 --> 00:13:19.691
Once a day.

00:13:20.008 --> 00:13:23.511
They use that thing over
there to open the cage.

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:26.055
And that's the only time you see them?

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:28.474
So far. But I'm waiting.

00:13:28.509 --> 00:13:30.410
Waiting for what?

00:13:30.445 --> 00:13:32.276
Their baiting time, man.

00:13:32.311 --> 00:13:34.536
I think that's the least
of your worries right now.

00:13:34.571 --> 00:13:35.303
Oh, yeah?

00:13:35.338 --> 00:13:35.738
Yeah.

00:13:35.773 --> 00:13:37.028
What do you they want then?

00:13:37.685 --> 00:13:39.575
Depends on who they are.

00:13:39.610 --> 00:13:42.613
They're bunch of psycho
hill-Billy red neck if you ask me.

00:13:42.648 --> 00:13:45.366
Looking for love in
all the wrong places.

00:13:59.752 --> 00:14:01.973
Okay, the next traffic cam

00:14:02.008 --> 00:14:05.595
Is fifty miles from here and your
pickup didn't pass that one. So...

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:07.572
So, it must have pulled up somewhere.

00:14:08.016 --> 00:14:09.480
I don't see any other roads here.

00:14:09.911 --> 00:14:14.020
Well, a lot of these back woods
properties have their own private roads.

00:14:14.523 --> 00:14:15.855
Great.

00:14:28.723 --> 00:14:30.077
So, Gregory.

00:14:30.593 --> 00:14:31.085
Yeah.

00:14:31.887 --> 00:14:33.128
I ran your badge number.

00:14:33.163 --> 00:14:35.860
It's routine when working
A case with State Police

00:14:35.895 --> 00:14:37.752
For county purposes when we have you.

00:14:38.445 --> 00:14:41.589
And they just got back to me...

00:14:45.213 --> 00:14:47.386
Says here your badge was stolen.

00:14:48.172 --> 00:14:51.377
And there's a picture of you.

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:57.425
I lost some weight.

00:14:57.460 --> 00:14:59.807
And I got that Michael
Jackson skin disease...

00:14:59.842 --> 00:15:00.585
Okay.

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:02.100
Would you step out of the car please?

00:15:02.135 --> 00:15:03.003
Look, look, look.

00:15:05.053 --> 00:15:07.222
If you want to arrest me that's fine.

00:15:07.257 --> 00:15:09.433
I'll cooperate. I swear.

00:15:09.468 --> 00:15:11.608
But first please...

00:15:11.643 --> 00:15:12.635
Let me find Sam.

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:14.192
I don't even know who you are.

00:15:14.514 --> 00:15:16.696
Or if this Sam person is missing.

00:15:16.731 --> 00:15:19.067
Look into my eyes and tell
me if I'm lying about this.

00:15:19.102 --> 00:15:22.561
Identity theft. You're
impersonating an officer.

00:15:23.607 --> 00:15:25.273
Here's the thing. When...

00:15:25.564 --> 00:15:27.416
When we were young...

00:15:27.451 --> 00:15:30.458
I pretty much pulled him from a fire.

00:15:31.496 --> 00:15:34.635
And ever since then I
felt responsible for him.

00:15:35.097 --> 00:15:38.628
You know, like it's my
job to keep him safe.

00:15:40.672 --> 00:15:44.968
I'm just afraid if we
don't find him fast.

00:15:45.927 --> 00:15:47.888
Please...

00:15:48.346 --> 00:15:51.308
He's my family.

00:15:52.100 --> 00:15:54.234
I'm sorry.

00:15:54.269 --> 00:15:56.730
You've given me no choice.

00:15:56.765 --> 00:15:59.191
I have to take you in.

00:16:12.897 --> 00:16:15.838
After we find Sam Winchester.

00:16:18.543 --> 00:16:20.072
What's your name again?

00:16:20.107 --> 00:16:21.382
It's Sam.

00:16:21.946 --> 00:16:25.325
Why won't you give it up
Sammy. There's no way out.

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:26.951
Don't...

00:16:27.535 --> 00:16:29.078
Call me...

00:16:29.113 --> 00:16:30.621
Sammy.

00:16:33.082 --> 00:16:35.460
What is it?

00:16:39.464 --> 00:16:40.805
It's a bracket.

00:16:40.840 --> 00:16:44.594
Well, thank God a bracket.
Now we got them, huh?

00:16:46.888 --> 00:16:49.474
Must have been a short.

00:16:52.226 --> 00:16:55.521
Maybe you knocked something loose.

00:16:58.399 --> 00:17:00.117
I think you should get
back in there Jenkins.

00:17:00.152 --> 00:17:00.711
What?

00:17:01.187 --> 00:17:02.869
This isn't right.

00:17:02.904 --> 00:17:04.885
Do you want to get out of here?

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:06.831
Yeah, but that was too easy.

00:17:06.866 --> 00:17:09.077
Look, I'm gonna get out of
here. I'm gonna send help. Okay?

00:17:09.112 --> 00:17:09.934
Okay. Don't worry.

00:17:09.969 --> 00:17:10.629
No.

00:17:10.664 --> 00:17:13.456
I'm serious, Jenkins.
This might be a trap.

00:17:13.491 --> 00:17:15.416
Bye, Sammy.

00:17:15.708 --> 00:17:17.627
Jenkins!

00:17:57.416 --> 00:17:59.376
Thank you.

00:19:32.444 --> 00:19:34.195
Okay, officer.

00:19:34.446 --> 00:19:36.021
Look I'm gonna press my luck.

00:19:36.056 --> 00:19:37.976
Your luck is so pressed.

00:19:38.276 --> 00:19:39.909
Right.

00:19:40.201 --> 00:19:42.078
I was wondering...

00:19:42.328 --> 00:19:44.726
Why are you helping me out anyway?

00:19:44.761 --> 00:19:47.125
Why don't you just lock me up?

00:19:48.042 --> 00:19:51.379
My brother Riley
disappeared three years ago.

00:19:51.414 --> 00:19:53.763
A lot like Sam.

00:19:53.798 --> 00:19:55.675
We searched for him but...

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:57.927
Nothing.

00:19:58.595 --> 00:20:01.514
I know what it's like to
feel responsible for someone.

00:20:01.549 --> 00:20:03.850
And for them...

00:20:06.436 --> 00:20:09.006
Come on, let's keep at it.

00:20:12.567 --> 00:20:14.792
Wait, wait. Pull over here. Pull over.

00:20:26.551 --> 00:20:28.718
It's the first turn
off I've seen so far.

00:20:29.792 --> 00:20:31.544
You stay here, I'll check it out.

00:20:31.579 --> 00:20:32.680
No way.

00:20:32.715 --> 00:20:33.781
Hey...

00:20:34.464 --> 00:20:36.278
You're a civilian.

00:20:36.313 --> 00:20:38.057
And a felon, I think.

00:20:38.092 --> 00:20:40.511
I'm not taking you with me.

00:20:41.037 --> 00:20:42.388
You're not going without me.

00:20:45.624 --> 00:20:47.775
All right. You promise...

00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:51.064
You won't get involved.
You let me handle it.

00:20:51.703 --> 00:20:53.041
Yeah, I promise.

00:20:53.076 --> 00:20:54.984
Shake on it.

00:20:58.911 --> 00:21:00.782
Oh, come on.

00:21:01.532 --> 00:21:03.833
This is ridiculous.

00:21:04.568 --> 00:21:06.612
Katherine, I really think
you're gonna need my help.

00:21:06.647 --> 00:21:09.990
I'll manage. Thank you.

00:21:13.452 --> 00:21:16.372
I got to start carrying paper clips.

00:21:46.985 --> 00:21:48.391
Hello?

00:21:51.615 --> 00:21:53.463
Anybody home?

00:22:08.424 --> 00:22:09.668
Hi.

00:22:11.009 --> 00:22:12.780
How are you?

00:22:18.559 --> 00:22:20.234
Who are you?

00:22:20.269 --> 00:22:24.565
I'm Katherine. I'm a deputy.

00:22:24.600 --> 00:22:26.608
What's your name?

00:22:26.643 --> 00:22:28.242
Missy.

00:22:28.277 --> 00:22:30.737
Missy? That's a pretty name.

00:22:30.772 --> 00:22:33.198
Missy, is your mom home?

00:22:33.233 --> 00:22:35.624
She's dead.

00:22:35.659 --> 00:22:39.496
I'm sorry, what about your dad?

00:22:39.788 --> 00:22:42.082
No?

00:22:43.125 --> 00:22:46.170
Can I come in for a minute?

00:22:46.587 --> 00:22:48.922
I just want you look at a picture.

00:22:48.957 --> 00:22:51.357
Have you seen that guy?

00:22:53.469 --> 00:22:55.825
Look at that picture.

00:22:57.848 --> 00:22:59.356
What?

00:22:59.391 --> 00:23:01.894
That's gonna hurt.

00:23:04.730 --> 00:23:06.363
Missy, sweetheart.

00:23:06.398 --> 00:23:08.901
Go tell your brothers,
I want to see them.

00:23:08.936 --> 00:23:11.487
Yes, daddy.

00:23:28.212 --> 00:23:30.589
Son of a bitch.

00:24:34.226 --> 00:24:36.467
But I've never seen him so angry before.

00:24:36.502 --> 00:24:39.783
Never been followed
by the police before.

00:24:54.830 --> 00:24:57.208
You all right?

00:25:00.252 --> 00:25:03.213
Are you Sam Winchester? Aren't you?

00:25:03.248 --> 00:25:05.003
Yeah.

00:25:05.038 --> 00:25:06.759
You're...

00:25:07.134 --> 00:25:10.471
You're cousin's looking for you.

00:25:11.555 --> 00:25:13.411
Thank God.

00:25:13.446 --> 00:25:15.482
Where is he?

00:25:15.517 --> 00:25:17.519
He uh...

00:25:17.853 --> 00:25:21.065
I cuffed him to my car.

00:25:42.670 --> 00:25:44.421
Sam?

00:25:45.047 --> 00:25:46.382
Are you hurt?

00:25:46.417 --> 00:25:48.133
No.

00:25:48.342 --> 00:25:50.844
Damn, it's good to see you.

00:25:51.595 --> 00:25:54.682
How did you get out of the cuffs?

00:25:54.717 --> 00:25:57.559
I know a trick or two.

00:25:58.560 --> 00:26:00.521
All right.

00:26:00.771 --> 00:26:02.231
Oh.

00:26:02.523 --> 00:26:04.865
These locks they're gonna be a bitch.

00:26:04.900 --> 00:26:08.112
Well, there's some kind of
automatic control. Right there.

00:26:08.347 --> 00:26:10.188
Have you seen them?

00:26:10.223 --> 00:26:11.488
Yeah.

00:26:11.523 --> 00:26:13.734
Dude, they're just people.

00:26:13.769 --> 00:26:15.826
And they jumped you?

00:26:15.861 --> 00:26:19.364
Must be getting a little
rusty there, kiddo.

00:26:19.399 --> 00:26:20.386
What do they want?

00:26:20.421 --> 00:26:21.150
I don't know.

00:26:21.151 --> 00:26:23.010
They let Jenkins go, but...

00:26:23.045 --> 00:26:24.835
That was some sort of trap.

00:26:24.870 --> 00:26:26.947
It doesn't make any sense to me.

00:26:26.982 --> 00:26:28.337
Oh, well that's the point.

00:26:28.372 --> 00:26:29.548
You know with...

00:26:29.583 --> 00:26:33.587
Our usual play mates there's rules,
here's patterns. But with people...

00:26:33.622 --> 00:26:35.429
They're just crazy.

00:26:35.464 --> 00:26:38.008
You see anything else out there?

00:26:38.800 --> 00:26:41.365
He has about a dozen junk cars
out back. Plates from all over.

00:26:41.400 --> 00:26:43.930
So, I'm thinking when they take
someone they take their car too.

00:26:43.965 --> 00:26:48.060
Did you see a black mustang?
Out there about ten years old?

00:26:48.095 --> 00:26:51.605
Yeah, actually I did.

00:26:53.281 --> 00:26:56.284
Your brothers?

00:26:57.494 --> 00:26:59.955
I'm sorry.

00:27:01.247 --> 00:27:04.334
Let's get you guys out of here. Then
we'll take care of those bastards.

00:27:04.369 --> 00:27:06.503
It takes a key, key?

00:27:06.538 --> 00:27:07.844
I don't know.

00:27:07.879 --> 00:27:09.756
All right, I better go find it.

00:27:09.791 --> 00:27:11.424
Hey.

00:27:11.800 --> 00:27:13.718
Be careful.

00:27:13.953 --> 00:27:15.920
Yeah.

00:28:27.325 --> 00:28:29.327
Well, I'll say it again.

00:28:29.362 --> 00:28:31.954
Demons I get.

00:28:32.121 --> 00:28:34.540
People are crazy.

00:29:24.420 --> 00:29:26.026
What the...

00:31:01.986 --> 00:31:04.656
It's okay. I'm not gonna hurt you.

00:31:04.989 --> 00:31:06.699
I know.

00:31:06.908 --> 00:31:08.201
Daddy!

00:31:08.326 --> 00:31:09.661
Daddy!

00:31:09.911 --> 00:31:11.454
Daddy!

00:31:12.080 --> 00:31:13.915
Daddy!

00:31:42.326 --> 00:31:45.413
I'm gonna kick your ass first.

00:31:45.746 --> 00:31:47.665
Then yours.

00:31:59.552 --> 00:32:01.345
Come on.

00:32:01.512 --> 00:32:02.895
Let's hunt.

00:32:02.930 --> 00:32:04.890
Yeah, this one's a fighter.

00:32:04.925 --> 00:32:07.893
Sure be fun to hunt.

00:32:08.561 --> 00:32:10.444
Oh, you got to be kidding me.

00:32:10.479 --> 00:32:12.565
This is what this is about? You...

00:32:12.600 --> 00:32:15.401
You yahoos hunt people?

00:32:16.902 --> 00:32:20.364
You ever killed before?

00:32:20.399 --> 00:32:22.366
What?

00:32:23.659 --> 00:32:26.287
Well, it depends on what you mean.

00:32:26.322 --> 00:32:29.630
I've hunted all my life.

00:32:29.665 --> 00:32:33.377
Just like my father, his before him.

00:32:33.412 --> 00:32:35.504
I've hunted deer...

00:32:35.539 --> 00:32:37.304
And bear...

00:32:37.339 --> 00:32:41.385
I even got a coo-Coo once. Oh boy.

00:32:41.802 --> 00:32:44.597
But the best hunt...

00:32:44.632 --> 00:32:47.099
Is human.

00:32:48.267 --> 00:32:51.068
Oh, there's nothing like it.

00:32:51.103 --> 00:32:55.573
Holding their life in your hands.

00:32:55.608 --> 00:33:00.529
Seeing the fear in their
eyes just before they go dark.

00:33:00.564 --> 00:33:04.450
Makes you feel powerful alive.

00:33:04.685 --> 00:33:07.403
You're a sick puppy.

00:33:08.070 --> 00:33:10.246
We give them a weapon.

00:33:10.281 --> 00:33:13.158
Give him a fighting chance.

00:33:13.393 --> 00:33:15.701
It's kind of like...

00:33:15.736 --> 00:33:18.745
Our tradition passed down

00:33:18.780 --> 00:33:24.001
Father to son, cost
only one or two a year.

00:33:24.036 --> 00:33:29.082
Never enough to bring the lot
down we've never been that sloppy.

00:33:29.117 --> 00:33:31.627
Yeah, well. Don't save yourself short.

00:33:31.662 --> 00:33:34.338
You're plenty of sloppy.

00:33:35.672 --> 00:33:39.635
So what? You're with that pretty cop?

00:33:44.932 --> 00:33:47.935
Are you a cop?

00:33:49.561 --> 00:33:52.112
If I tell you...

00:33:52.147 --> 00:33:56.026
You promise not to make
me into an ash tray?

00:34:00.288 --> 00:34:03.875
Only reason I don't let my
boys take you right here now

00:34:03.910 --> 00:34:07.385
Is that there's
something I need to know.

00:34:07.420 --> 00:34:10.206
Yeah, how about it's not
nice to marry your sister.

00:34:11.077 --> 00:34:16.763
Tell me, any of the cops
go come looking for you?

00:34:16.798 --> 00:34:18.104
Oh, eat me.

00:34:18.139 --> 00:34:21.434
No, no, no. Wait. You actually might.

00:34:23.937 --> 00:34:26.821
You think this is funny?

00:34:26.856 --> 00:34:30.777
You've brought this down on my family.

00:34:32.520 --> 00:34:34.487
All right?

00:34:34.522 --> 00:34:37.546
You want to play games?

00:34:37.581 --> 00:34:40.570
We'll play some games.

00:34:42.864 --> 00:34:47.577
Looks like we're gonna have a
hunt tonight after all, boys.

00:34:47.612 --> 00:34:50.663
And you get to pick the animal.

00:34:50.698 --> 00:34:53.037
The boy or the cop.

00:34:53.072 --> 00:34:55.376
Okay, wait, wait.

00:34:55.960 --> 00:34:58.838
Look, nobody's coming for
me. All right? It's just us.

00:34:58.873 --> 00:35:02.091
You don't choose, I will.

00:35:03.635 --> 00:35:07.055
Oh, you son of a bitch!

00:35:11.726 --> 00:35:14.402
Next time, I'll take an eye.

00:35:14.437 --> 00:35:18.233
All right, all right. The
guy. The guy. Take the guy!

00:35:18.858 --> 00:35:20.617
Lee.

00:35:20.952 --> 00:35:23.412
Go do it.

00:35:23.955 --> 00:35:26.561
Don't let him out though.

00:35:26.596 --> 00:35:29.168
Shoot him in the cage.

00:35:30.294 --> 00:35:32.338
What?

00:35:32.547 --> 00:35:34.323
I thought you said you
were gonna hunt him.

00:35:34.358 --> 00:35:35.589
You're gonna give him a chance!

00:35:35.624 --> 00:35:37.161
Lee!

00:35:37.196 --> 00:35:39.053
When you're done with the boy.

00:35:39.088 --> 00:35:42.014
Shoot the bitch too.

00:35:44.350 --> 00:35:49.814
We're cleaning this mess up before
any more cops come running out here.

00:35:58.614 --> 00:36:00.491
What are you doing?

00:36:08.624 --> 00:36:09.792
Hey!

00:36:11.836 --> 00:36:14.297
You hurt my brother,
I'll kill you. I swear.

00:36:14.332 --> 00:36:16.712
I'll kill you all.

00:36:16.747 --> 00:36:19.093
I will kill you all!

00:36:19.768 --> 00:36:21.645
Lee!

00:36:31.822 --> 00:36:33.490
Damn.

00:36:38.704 --> 00:36:40.372
Lee!

00:36:42.541 --> 00:36:45.210
Jack, you come with me.

00:36:45.245 --> 00:36:46.670
Missy.

00:36:46.879 --> 00:36:49.298
You watch him now.

00:36:58.140 --> 00:36:59.350
Lee?

00:36:59.641 --> 00:37:01.393
Where are you?

00:37:05.439 --> 00:37:06.899
Lee?

00:37:08.976 --> 00:37:11.562
Damn it. Jack, hit the lights.

00:37:12.896 --> 00:37:15.315
They must have pulled the fuses.

00:38:46.857 --> 00:38:48.558
You stupid...

00:38:49.559 --> 00:38:50.810
Hey!

00:39:26.762 --> 00:39:28.723
I'll watch this one. You go ahead.

00:39:33.402 --> 00:39:35.988
Go ahead.

00:39:46.457 --> 00:39:48.883
You hurt my family.

00:39:48.918 --> 00:39:51.441
I'm gonna bleed you bitch.

00:39:51.476 --> 00:39:53.965
You killed my brother.

00:39:54.000 --> 00:39:56.342
Your brother?

00:39:57.552 --> 00:39:59.435
Now I see.

00:39:59.470 --> 00:40:02.056
Just tell me why.

00:40:03.567 --> 00:40:06.310
Because it's fun.

00:40:29.174 --> 00:40:29.988
Where's the girl?

00:40:30.023 --> 00:40:31.391
I locked her in the closet.

00:40:31.426 --> 00:40:33.553
What about the dad?

00:40:35.180 --> 00:40:38.809
Shot. Trying to escape.

00:40:49.444 --> 00:40:52.697
I think the car's at the police station.

00:40:52.864 --> 00:40:56.159
Backup units on route to your location.

00:40:58.745 --> 00:41:00.580
So...

00:41:00.914 --> 00:41:04.209
State Police and the FBI are
gonna be here within the hour.

00:41:04.244 --> 00:41:07.128
They're gonna want to talk to you.

00:41:07.629 --> 00:41:11.925
I suggest that you're
both long gone by then.

00:41:12.092 --> 00:41:13.927
Thanks.

00:41:16.137 --> 00:41:17.910
Hey, listen. I don't
mean to press our luck.

00:41:17.945 --> 00:41:19.683
But we're kind of in
the middle of nowhere.

00:41:19.718 --> 00:41:22.060
You think we could catch a ride?

00:41:22.095 --> 00:41:24.354
Start walking.

00:41:25.438 --> 00:41:27.857
Duck if you see a SWAT car.

00:41:27.892 --> 00:41:30.277
Sounds great to me. Thanks.

00:41:30.986 --> 00:41:32.904
Listen...

00:41:34.639 --> 00:41:37.433
I'm sorry about your brother.

00:41:37.892 --> 00:41:39.894
Thank you.

00:41:41.229 --> 00:41:42.779
It was really hard not
knowing what happened to him.

00:41:42.814 --> 00:41:48.319
I thought it would be easier
once I knew the truth. But...

00:41:49.445 --> 00:41:51.864
It isn't really.

00:41:56.703 --> 00:41:59.330
Anyway you should go.

00:42:12.593 --> 00:42:15.096
Don't ever do that again.

00:42:15.131 --> 00:42:16.270
Do what?

00:42:16.305 --> 00:42:18.266
Go missing like that.

00:42:19.684 --> 00:42:21.978
You were worried about me.

00:42:22.729 --> 00:42:26.399
I'm saying, you vanish like that
again I'm not looking for you.

00:42:26.691 --> 00:42:27.711
Sure you will.

00:42:27.746 --> 00:42:28.468
I'm not.

00:42:29.318 --> 00:42:31.577
So you got saddled on by
a 13 year old girl, huh?

00:42:31.612 --> 00:42:32.598
Oh, shut up!

00:42:32.633 --> 00:42:34.570
Just saying getting rusty there, kiddo.

00:42:35.116 --> 00:42:36.784
Shut up!



